==================================================

The backend currently runs locally on the Mac.

A real iPhone cannot reach the Mac backend through:

127.0.0.1
localhost

because those addresses point to the iPhone itself.

Configure the backend development server so it can accept connections from the local network, for example by binding Fastify to:

0.0.0.0

Do not weaken production security settings.

For DEVELOPMENT ONLY, configure the iOS app with a development API base URL that points to the Mac's LAN IP address and backend port.

Do not hard-code the IP throughout the codebase.

Create one central API configuration layer, for example:

API_BASE_URL

so we can later replace the local Mac address with the production server URL.

Document clearly where I change this value.

Do not expose database credentials to the iPhone.

